#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096479 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096680 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ffce8b3-cc12-5a4d-88fd-77889b6bdd3f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Trigonometric Expression Using the Tabular Method of Integration by Parts"}] :question/id #uuid "f4bca758-9903-505c-9828-0e1788b25d9f" :question/math-academy-id "e-499" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int (x^4-3x) \\cos(x) \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "For this integral we choose $u = x^4-3x$ and $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\cos(x).$ Filling in the table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} x^4-3x$ | $\\cos(x)$ |  |  |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} 4x^3-3$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} \\sin(x)$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} +$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} (x^4-3x)\\sin(x)$ |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} 12x^2$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06}   -\\cos(x)$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} -$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06}  -(4x^3-3)(-\\cos(x))$ |\n| $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1} 24x$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1}  -\\sin(x)$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} +$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} 12x^2(-\\sin(x))$ |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0,0.5,1} 24$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1} \\cos(x)$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1} -$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1}- 24x\\cos(x)$ |\n| $0$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0.5,1}  \\sin(x)$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0.5,1}+$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0.5,1}  24\\sin(x)$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{4}-3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =({x}^{4}-3x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+(4{x}^{3}-3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & \\,\\,-12{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-24x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+24\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C \\\\  & =({x}^{4}-12{x}^{2}-3x+24)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & \\,\\,+(4{x}^{3}-24x-3)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096482 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096681 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "708faaf1-be43-502c-88dc-94270e8783b6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Algebraic and Exponential Expressions Using the Tabular Method of Integration by Parts"}] :question/id #uuid "96f1c791-f1cd-5a20-a6ee-004475bbd482" :question/math-academy-id "e-500" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int (x^2-1)(x+2)^5 \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "For this integral, we choose $u = x^2-1$ and $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x} =(x+2)^5.$ Filling in our table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} x^2-1$ | $(x+2)^5$ |  |  |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} 2x$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\\dfrac{(x+2)^6}{6}$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} +$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\\dfrac{(x^2-1)(x+2)^6}{6}$ |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} 2$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} \\dfrac{(x+2)^7}{42}$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} -$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} -\\,\\dfrac{x(x+2)^7}{21}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\\dfrac{(x+2)^8}{336}$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} +$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1}  \\dfrac{(x+2)^8}{168}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{2}-1)(x+2)^{5}\\text{d}x & =\\frac{({x}^{2}-1)(x+2)^{6}}{6}-\\frac{x(x+2)^{7}}{21}+\\frac{(x+2)^{8}}{168}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+2)^{6}}{168}(28({x}^{2}-1)-8x(x+2)+(x+2)^{2})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+2)^{6}}{168}(21{x}^{2}-12x-24)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548032 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096680 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ffce8b3-cc12-5a4d-88fd-77889b6bdd3f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Trigonometric Expression Using the Tabular Method of Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29b846ea-2b46-5827-9dc6-ab58e3d774a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3x-2{x}^{3})\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+(6{x}^{2}-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547396} {:answer/id #uuid "7bf18243-7d6d-542d-ad2a-119fd8b14886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2{x}^{3}-3x)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+(6{x}^{2}-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547585} {:answer/id #uuid "8d1726c2-0aa9-5f31-897a-f88a2c0ffb38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3-2{x}^{3})\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+(6{x}^{2}+3x)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547631} {:answer/id #uuid "a5d2c5ff-d684-5446-84ee-0690faaf6e16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6x-2{x}^{3})\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+(3{x}^{2}+3)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547681} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e0fbd8-18b1-5bd2-b17a-95a9d13ac705" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2{x}^{3}-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+(6{x}^{2}+3x)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29b846ea-2b46-5827-9dc6-ab58e3d774a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3x-2{x}^{3})\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+(6{x}^{2}-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547396} :answer-field/id #uuid "76d3aaee-ce69-5796-b3e2-8ab1f761af18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547901}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "98841fb8-b49b-5f0b-816e-9b78835d046c" :question/math-academy-id "q-104069" :question/problem "$\\int 2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "For this integral we choose $u=2{x}^{3}$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x).$ Filling in the table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2{x}^{3}$ | $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ |  |  |\n| $6{x}^{2}$ | $-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}$ | $+$ | $-{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ |\n| $12x$ | $-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}$ | $-$ | $\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}$ |\n| $12$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{16}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{3x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}-\\frac{3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C \\\\  & =(3x-2{x}^{3})\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+(6{x}^{2}-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096681 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "708faaf1-be43-502c-88dc-94270e8783b6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Algebraic and Exponential Expressions Using the Tabular Method of Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37217c9b-33b1-59e4-b8aa-0211d9f120e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(2{x}^{3}+6x+5)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547431} {:answer/id #uuid "3c9a9114-317c-5b9b-a420-60d067c6ad9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}(3{x}^{3}+5x+6)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547450} {:answer/id #uuid "4a297628-b2be-5be8-9320-fbed23850259" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(2{x}^{3}+5)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547481} {:answer/id #uuid "9f924e65-5270-528b-9b33-05c8467a19f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(5{x}^{3}+2)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547663} {:answer/id #uuid "a3cb7fc1-c60e-51fb-be11-25aba8dc3e0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}({x}^{3}+2x+5)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a297628-b2be-5be8-9320-fbed23850259" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(2{x}^{3}+5)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547481} :answer-field/id #uuid "a255b420-3e67-5961-b79f-82039635a315" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547919}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1051456d-d936-5dd0-8e18-6d4a40dca9fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-13146" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\int (2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "For this integral, we choose $u=2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{2x}.$ Filling in our table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5$ | ${e}^{2x}$ |  |  |\n| $6{x}^{2}+6x$ | $\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{(2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x}}{2}$ |\n| $12x+6$ | $\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{(3{x}^{2}+3x){e}^{2x}}{2}$ |\n| $12$ | $\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{8}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{(6x+3){e}^{2x}}{4}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{16}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{3{e}^{2x}}{4}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}[2(2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5)-2(3{x}^{2}+3x)+(6x+3)-3]+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}(4{x}^{3}+10)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(2{x}^{3}+5)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548049 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096681 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "708faaf1-be43-502c-88dc-94270e8783b6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Algebraic and Exponential Expressions Using the Tabular Method of Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c546568-626b-5cd6-b8ac-d2575386f3be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{81}(27{x}^{4}-27{x}^{3}+36{x}^{2}+20x-20)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547403} {:answer/id #uuid "3b221da8-82dd-5c78-adf8-f6dfced47edc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{3x}}{27}(27{x}^{4}+36{x}^{3}-36{x}^{2}+10x-20)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547443} {:answer/id #uuid "5ef12b2d-3da6-5428-8177-102eeef66d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{27}(27{x}^{4}+36{x}^{3}-36{x}^{2}+30x-10)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547524} {:answer/id #uuid "6da2e75c-0701-5b79-a64c-adc247058072" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{3x}}{81}(27{x}^{4}-36{x}^{3}+36{x}^{2}+30x-10)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547561} {:answer/id #uuid "fd8ab7a4-bb1c-5998-ba3f-50e0b6ba5816" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{81}(20{x}^{4}+36{x}^{3}+36{x}^{2}+10x-27)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6da2e75c-0701-5b79-a64c-adc247058072" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{3x}}{81}(27{x}^{4}-36{x}^{3}+36{x}^{2}+30x-10)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547561} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb054bd7-c812-50e0-88f0-5e700282b833" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c451ec1c-6a2b-54c4-80d7-187b41f5f298" :question/math-academy-id "q-13147" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\int (2{x}^{4}+4x){e}^{3x}\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "For this integral, we choose $u=2{x}^{4}+4x$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{3x}.$ Filling in our table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2{x}^{4}+4x$ | ${e}^{3x}$ |  |  |\n| $8{x}^{3}+4$ | $\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{(2{x}^{4}+4x){e}^{3x}}{3}$ |\n| $24{x}^{2}$ | $\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{(8{x}^{3}+4){e}^{3x}}{9}$ |\n| $48x$ | $\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{27}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{8{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{9}$ |\n| $48$ | $\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{81}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{16x{e}^{3x}}{27}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{243}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{16{e}^{3x}}{81}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{x}^{4}+4x){e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{81}(27(2{x}^{4}+4x)-9(8{x}^{3}+4)+9(8{x}^{2})-3(16x)+16)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{81}(54{x}^{4}-72{x}^{3}+72{x}^{2}+60x-20)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{3x}}{81}(27{x}^{4}-36{x}^{3}+36{x}^{2}+30x-10)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548035 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096680 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ffce8b3-cc12-5a4d-88fd-77889b6bdd3f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Trigonometric Expression Using the Tabular Method of Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fb41b18-d048-58ff-98b7-bb9707adb4b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-6x-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+(6{x}^{2}+12x-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547350} {:answer/id #uuid "14773948-f875-5444-af95-b23c3eec6adb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-3x-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+(2{x}^{2}+2x-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547358} {:answer/id #uuid "3490e7a3-ef90-5f58-baf3-34df7d8081b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+3x-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{8}+(3{x}^{2}+12x-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547424} {:answer/id #uuid "884ddcaf-f8cf-537c-baf0-530ad493bfa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-3x-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+(6{x}^{2}+12x-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547612} {:answer/id #uuid "9b1532f8-ad6a-57a3-b5ef-b39dbdab9a20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-3x+3)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}-(6{x}^{2}+2x-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "884ddcaf-f8cf-537c-baf0-530ad493bfa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-3x-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+(6{x}^{2}+12x-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547612} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9c7956f-34b4-5bbc-822d-999232812733" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547965}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9ecd3f37-138d-5c59-a588-9da4d5939fe0" :question/math-academy-id "q-13148" :question/problem "$\\int ({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "For this integral we choose $u={x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).$ Filling in the table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}$ | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ |  |  |\n| $3{x}^{2}+6x$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}$ |\n| $6x+6$ | $-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}$ | $-$ | $\\frac{(3{x}^{2}+6x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}$ |\n| $6$ | $-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{8}$ | $+$ | $-\\frac{(3x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{16}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{({x}^{3}+3{x}^{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{(3{x}^{2}+6x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{(3x+3)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C \\\\  & =(2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-3x-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+(6{x}^{2}+12x-3)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548028 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096680 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ffce8b3-cc12-5a4d-88fd-77889b6bdd3f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Trigonometric Expression Using the Tabular Method of Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "361558e0-b03e-5e24-b859-1780cbf73441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+12x+5)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+(6{x}^{2}+6-12)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547427} {:answer/id #uuid "68f021c7-4684-5f75-a7e6-7bf59db64272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+12x+5)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-(6{x}^{2}+6+12)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547548} {:answer/id #uuid "ae8b2753-6527-5ff7-8bf6-5f58489ba3f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+12x+11)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-(6{x}^{2}+6x+12)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547697} {:answer/id #uuid "b5d77f24-72e3-5890-b26e-03347b9837a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+12x+11)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+(6{x}^{2}+6x-12)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547710} {:answer/id #uuid "f7dc74ed-d99f-5379-bc5f-c05c0291af00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-12x-1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+(6{x}^{2}+6x-12)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7dc74ed-d99f-5379-bc5f-c05c0291af00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-12x-1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+(6{x}^{2}+6x-12)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547820} :answer-field/id #uuid "93ab3dbe-b63d-5c2c-ad07-9ef67d064f5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547912}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8eec90d6-f38c-50f0-b171-7f37a87f27a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-14755" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\int (2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "For this integral, we choose $u=2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).$ Filling in the table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same Color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5$ | $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ |  |  |\n| $6{x}^{2}+6x$ | $-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)$ | $+$ | $-(2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)$ |\n| $12x+6$ | $-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ | $-$ | $(6{x}^{2}+6x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ |\n| $12$ | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)$ | $+$ | $(12x+6)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)$ |\n| $0$ | $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ | $-$ | $-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-(2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+5)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+(6{x}^{2}+6x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,+(12x+6)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C \\\\  & =-(2{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}-12x-1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,+(6{x}^{2}+6x-12)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548060 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096681 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "708faaf1-be43-502c-88dc-94270e8783b6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Algebraic and Exponential Expressions Using the Tabular Method of Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "076b789d-51b5-5ef9-a0dd-ba86934844f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{64}(32{x}^{4}+32{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547332} {:answer/id #uuid "08b769a9-d021-5cbd-b502-3820d8cbbf8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{64}(32{x}^{4}+32{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}+12x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547335} {:answer/id #uuid "36069d7a-e480-58f6-be3e-69f4a2e0c58c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{64}(32{x}^{4}-32{x}^{3}-24{x}^{2}-12x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547426} {:answer/id #uuid "699fea69-ada0-5282-b189-fe6c0c7e43e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{8}(32{x}^{4}+32{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547551} {:answer/id #uuid "ce6586a5-0ad1-53d1-b303-ca7e81cc40e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{64}(32{x}^{4}-32{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce6586a5-0ad1-53d1-b303-ca7e81cc40e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{64}(32{x}^{4}-32{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x+3)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547759} :answer-field/id #uuid "505aa8f0-52fb-5012-93ff-9c404d373469" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547881}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d35b604c-10fb-5e20-9163-ae0fba981c99" :question/math-academy-id "q-14773" :question/problem "$\\int 2{x}^{4}{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "For this integral, we choose $u=2{x}^{4}$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x}.$ Filling in our table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2{x}^{4}$ | ${e}^{4x}$ |  |  |\n| $8{x}^{3}$ | $\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{{x}^{4}{e}^{4x}}{2}$ |\n| $24{x}^{2}$ | $\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{{x}^{3}{e}^{4x}}{2}$ |\n| $48x$ | $\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{64}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{3{x}^{2}{e}^{4x}}{8}$ |\n| $48$ | $\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{256}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{3x{e}^{4x}}{16}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{1024}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{3{e}^{4x}}{64}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\int 2{x}^{4}{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{64}(32{x}^{4}-32{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-12x+3)+C\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547973 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096681 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "708faaf1-be43-502c-88dc-94270e8783b6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Algebraic and Exponential Expressions Using the Tabular Method of Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f14705c-d59b-5e2c-861c-36f4631d9fef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(2{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-6x+5)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547376} {:answer/id #uuid "3e44753e-7b3a-546a-9430-d898f8a54dff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(4{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-6x-5)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547455} {:answer/id #uuid "42ed1c85-2087-5131-92d7-96af891136fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}(4{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-6x+5)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547463} {:answer/id #uuid "75d02ccf-1668-5386-b753-447c7b62662e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}({x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-6x-5)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547572} {:answer/id #uuid "a29d9de4-509e-52f0-ac23-c5a30d5ee00e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}(2{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+6x+5)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f14705c-d59b-5e2c-861c-36f4631d9fef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(2{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-6x+5)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547376} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb590fe5-81e6-56d3-a58f-ef57c7889ade" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547945}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09b2a1cb-b590-5e4c-af65-76fb35a22b46" :question/math-academy-id "q-14778" :question/problem "$\\int (4{x}^{4}+4){e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "For this integral, we choose $u=4{x}^{4}+4$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{2x}.$ Filling in our table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4{x}^{4}+4$ | ${e}^{2x}$ |  |  |\n| $16{x}^{3}$ | $\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{2}$ | $+$ | $(2{x}^{4}+2){e}^{2x}$ |\n| $48{x}^{2}$ | $\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{4}$ | $-$ | $-4{x}^{3}{e}^{2x}$ |\n| $96x$ | $\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{8}$ | $+$ | $6{x}^{2}{e}^{2x}$ |\n| $96$ | $\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{16}$ | $-$ | $-6x{e}^{2x}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{32}$ | $+$ | $3{e}^{2x}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4{x}^{4}+4){e}^{2x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={e}^{2x}(2{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-6x+5)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548067 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096680 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ffce8b3-cc12-5a4d-88fd-77889b6bdd3f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Trigonometric Expression Using the Tabular Method of Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05134a4e-1d46-5e28-bcb2-8f6817ff28b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(54{x}^{4}-72{x}^{2}+124)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{81}+(24{x}^{3}-16x)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{27}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547329} {:answer/id #uuid "390e73d9-b00b-5113-9cbc-0e77d9eab6a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(54{x}^{4}-72{x}^{2}+124)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{9}-(24{x}^{3}-16x)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{27}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547435} {:answer/id #uuid "439e49ca-de2e-54e0-8438-a3db1cbd3a97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(24{x}^{3}-16x)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{81}+(54{x}^{4}-72{x}^{2}-108)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{27}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547466} {:answer/id #uuid "e1556d1d-7c0b-58f7-b139-bfdb8d52f9cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(54{x}^{4}-72{x}^{2}-124)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{81}-(24{x}^{3}+16x)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{81}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547786} {:answer/id #uuid "e68095d8-230d-514b-a348-4ecdb6bd3857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(54{x}^{4}-72{x}^{2}-4)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{27}+(24{x}^{3}-16x)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{27}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05134a4e-1d46-5e28-bcb2-8f6817ff28b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(54{x}^{4}-72{x}^{2}+124)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{81}+(24{x}^{3}-16x)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{27}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547329} :answer-field/id #uuid "94678b2e-f715-53b9-be25-66d1e2519658" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e3b2de25-1eea-5c88-bd03-1de1fe67ccfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-14779" :question/problem "Evaluate  $\\int (2{x}^{4}+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "For this integral we choose $u=2{x}^{4}+4$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x).$ Filling in the table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2{x}^{4}+4$ | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)$ |  |  |\n| $8{x}^{3}$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{(2{x}^{4}+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}$ |\n| $24{x}^{2}$ | $-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}$ | $-$ | $\\frac{8{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}$ |\n| $48x$ | $-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{27}$ | $+$ | $-\\frac{8{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{9}$ |\n| $48$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{81}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{16x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{27}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{243}$ | $+$ | $\\frac{16\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{81}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2{x}^{4}+4)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(2{x}^{4}+4)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{8{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}-\\frac{8{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{9}-\\frac{16x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{27}+\\frac{16\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{81}+C \\\\  & =(54{x}^{4}-72{x}^{2}+124)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{81}+(24{x}^{3}-16x)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{27}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097127 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096681 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "708faaf1-be43-502c-88dc-94270e8783b6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Algebraic and Exponential Expressions Using the Tabular Method of Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b88c051-a025-5f03-81cf-5494a62f33da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}(4{x}^{4}+16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-96x+98)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547340} {:answer/id #uuid "1373c2fd-f8d9-5a55-b2e7-b4367c914f89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}(3{x}^{4}-12{x}^{3}-48{x}^{2}-96x+98)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547354} {:answer/id #uuid "68f9d3d4-6045-5de5-b395-cca423699609" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}(3{x}^{4}-12{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-96x-98)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547549} {:answer/id #uuid "88ff090e-80df-57fe-8d25-0fb774b1e7c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2x}(3{x}^{4}-12{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-96x+98)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547613} {:answer/id #uuid "e58ebe67-39f1-5846-88c9-622447a7af20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}(4{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-96x+98)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e58ebe67-39f1-5846-88c9-622447a7af20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}(4{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-96x+98)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547791} :answer-field/id #uuid "10bf188f-45f0-56ee-9364-6499de462127" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89395e95-1dd7-5374-9986-857a303ac379" :question/math-academy-id "q-14780" :question/problem "Evaluate  $\\int (4{x}^{4}+2){e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "For this integral, we choose $u=4{x}^{4}+2$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}.$ Filling in our table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $4{x}^{4}+2$ | ${e}^{x}$ |  |  |\n| $16{x}^{3}$ | ${e}^{x}$ | $+$ | $(4{x}^{4}+2){e}^{x}$ |\n| $48{x}^{2}$ | ${e}^{x}$ | $-$ | $-16{x}^{3}{e}^{x}$ |\n| $96x$ | ${e}^{x}$ | $+$ | $48{x}^{2}{e}^{x}$ |\n| $96$ | ${e}^{x}$ | $-$ | $-96x{e}^{x}$ |\n| $0$ | ${e}^{x}$ | $+$ | $96{e}^{x}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (4{x}^{4}+2){e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={e}^{x}(4{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-96x+98)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096680 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ffce8b3-cc12-5a4d-88fd-77889b6bdd3f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Trigonometric Expression Using the Tabular Method of Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "005d8792-e152-5779-a4e7-ff8164391a13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(6{x}^{2}-1)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}-(2{x}^{3}-x)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547316} {:answer/id #uuid "83cad23b-d2d2-5f7a-8af5-d4529b74ddaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2{x}^{3}-x)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{8}-(6{x}^{2}-1)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547598} {:answer/id #uuid "966a42f3-8914-57ac-ad7f-d4838065bee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6{x}^{2}-1)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+(2{x}^{3}-x)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547646} {:answer/id #uuid "dfadc85c-1a86-5b47-bbad-10d6a3d54487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2{x}^{3}-x)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+(6{x}^{2}-1)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547781} {:answer/id #uuid "fa42dddb-d508-5d72-99c7-43e829f72eb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-(2{x}^{3}-x)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}-(6{x}^{2}-1)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfadc85c-1a86-5b47-bbad-10d6a3d54487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2{x}^{3}-x)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+(6{x}^{2}-1)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547781} :answer-field/id #uuid "5647034f-2aaf-5579-99cc-ba72d358adba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547884}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1627a960-4b89-5682-9e7a-8ebccade355e" :question/math-academy-id "q-51229" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\int ({x}^{3}+x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "For this integral we choose $u={x}^{3}+x$ and $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x).$ Filling in the table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{3}+x$ | $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ |  |  |\n| $3{x}^{2}+1$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}$ | $+$ | $({x}^{3}+x)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}$ |\n| $6x$ | $-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}$ | $-$ | $(3{x}^{2}+1)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}$ |\n| $6$ | $-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{8}$ | $+$ | $-\\frac{3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{16}$ | $-$ | $-\\frac{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral. \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{3}+x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =({x}^{3}+x)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+(3{x}^{2}+1)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{3x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}-\\frac{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C \\\\  & =(2{x}^{3}-x)\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{4}+(6{x}^{2}-1)\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
